Article 25 During the existence of the marital relationship, the following property shall be classified as "other property that shall be jointly owned" under Article 1062 of the Civil Code:
(1) Income derived from a party's investment of personal property;
(2) Housing subsidies and housing provident funds actually obtained or due to be obtained by the man and the woman;
(3) Basic pensions and bankruptcy resettlement compensations actually obtained or due to be obtained by the man and the woman.

Article 44 Where a divorce case involves the raising of a minor child, the child under the age of two shall be handled in accordance with the principles stipulated in paragraph 3 of Article 1084 of the Civil Code. If the mother has one of the following circumstances, and the father requests direct raising of the child, the People's Court shall support such a request:
(1) The mother suffers from a contagious disease that is difficult to cure or another serious disease, making it inappropriate for the child to live with her;
(2) The mother has the conditions to raise the child but fails to perform the obligation of raising, and the father requests that the child live with him;
(3) For other reasons, the child is truly unsuitable to live with the mother.

Article 46 For a minor child who has reached the age of two, where both parents request direct custody, priority may be given to one party under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The party has undergone sterilization surgery or has lost fertility due to other reasons;
(2) The child has lived with the party for a relatively long period, and a change in the living environment would be clearly detrimental to the child's healthy growth;
(3) The party has no other children, while the other party has other children;
(4) The child living with the party is beneficial to the child's growth, while the other party suffers from a contagious disease that is difficult to cure or another serious disease, or has other circumstances detrimental to the child's physical and mental health, making it unsuitable for the child to live with the other party.

Article 56 Under any of the following circumstances, where one parent requests a change in the child custody arrangement, the People's Court shall support such a request:
(1) The parent living with the child is unable to continue raising the child due to a serious illness or disability;
(2) The parent living with the child fails to perform the obligation of raising the child, abuses the child, or the cohabitation has a clear adverse effect on the child's physical and mental health;
(3) The child, who has reached the age of eight, wishes to live with the other parent and that parent has the capacity to raise the child;
(4) There are other legitimate reasons requiring a change.

Article 58 Under any of the following circumstances, where a child requests an increase in child support from the parent who has the capacity to pay, the People's Court shall support such a request:
(1) The originally determined amount of child support is insufficient to maintain the local actual standard of living;
(2) Due to the child's illness or schooling, the actual needs have exceeded the originally determined amount;
(3) There are other legitimate reasons warranting an increase.
